WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.490
In 1961, the US unemployment
rate was 6.7 percent.

2
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:09.700
By 1969, it had fallen to 3.5 percent.

3
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.170
But over the same years,

4
00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.810
inflation climbed from about
1 percent to 5.5 percent.

5
00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:19.190
So can a country buy lower
unemployment by accepting

6
00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:20.850
a little more inflation?

7
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.970
In this mission, you'll
connect the AD and AS graph

8
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.490
to a new curve, step by step.

9
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.400
Then you'll use a graph lab:

10
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.350
slide unemployment down and
watch what happens to inflation.

11
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.580
Your mission: figure out
whether that trade-off is real,

12
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.490
and whether a country can count on it.
